[[ plugin_summary ]]

A plugin for [Heinzelmännchen](https://github.com/[[ heinzel_owner ]]/heinzel), an open-source crew of AI helpers that drafts a team's busywork.


## Install

Start the standard app with `uvx heinzel@latest`; it installs its default plugins automatically.
In another terminal, add this optional plugin:

```bash
hz system plugin add https://github.com/[[ github_owner ]]/[[ project_name ]] --confirm
```

Installation history records its resolved source. `hz system update` keeps compatible plugins;
`hz system plugin remove [[ project_name ]]` removes this one.

## Use

```bash
hz [[ plugin_name ]] info                 # this plugin, its version and the Heinzelmännchen it runs on
hz [[ plugin_name ]] hello --name Ada     # a submodule collapsed into a command
hz [[ plugin_name ]] info --json          # every command speaks JSON, for scripts and agents
hz system info                  # includes a section contributed by this plugin
```

## Documentation

[docs/plugins/[[ project_name ]]/index.md](docs/plugins/[[ project_name ]]/index.md) is this plugin's page: what it
brings in every head, its settings, credentials, themes and recordings, generated from the installed plugin by
`hz system plugin docs build` (`make fix` writes it, `make check` fails while it is missing or stale).
`make docs-record` records the scenes of [docs/scenes.toml](docs/scenes.toml) beside it, and `make docs-site` builds
the site the Docs workflow publishes on release.

## Develop

```bash
git init -b main # only for this standalone repository, never inside a plugin collection
make setup     # everything the build needs, and the git hooks; you need only git, make and uv
make fix       # create the lock and generated plugin reference
make doctor    # what is missing, and the command that fixes it
make preview   # this plugin and its installed core, with isolated app state
make check     # lint, types, unit + integration tests
make test-e2e  # installs Heinzelmännchen with uv and adds this checkout as a plugin
```

The starter contributes a status item, header action, sidebar item, Today widget, local panel and an explicit
`hz [[ plugin_name ]] notify` operation. Their priorities live beside their declarations. The static view in
`src/[[ package_name ]]/views/` needs no JavaScript build. `sdk/index.d.ts` describes its versioned host contract;
`hz system plugin sdk <new-directory>` exports current SDK types and runtime bridges for a larger bundled view.
Restart preview after changing built view assets. `make build` packages only this plugin.

The modules live in `src/[[ package_name ]]/`. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) and
[docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md](docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md) before changing them; the reviewer agents and hooks in
`.claude/` enforce them.

## Release

`make release INTRO="Describe this plugin release."` (or Actions → **Prepare release** → Run workflow) opens a release pull request on GitHub. A maintainer reviews it and its current-head checks before merging; merging tags and publishes. The version comes
from conventional commits, the changelog from git-cliff; the GitHub release carries the wheel, the sdist and
provenance attestations. `main` changes only through pull requests.

Add the topic `heinzel-plugin` to the GitHub repository so `hz system plugin search` lists the plugin.

